{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>And HaShem did not hear your voice.</b> Because of the desecration of the Name that they committed, for which no repentance suffices except mortifying death. And there was also a decree accompanied by oath, after Moses, Joshua, and Caleb awakened their ears to repentance and they did not repent even afterward except out of fear of punishment. Therefore their repentance did not suffice to remove the punishment decreed for this world — as was the case with Cain (Genesis 4:15), with Saul regarding Amalek (I Samuel 15:26), and with the sons of Eli (I Samuel 3:14)." "<b>And He did not listen to you.</b> Even to delay, let alone to annul, the decree upon the children, even after the death of the fathers. By this He proved to them that their repentance was not complete, and therefore they achieved nothing, even with their tears."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:12.088618400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}